speechtext:
That is difficult to do. I can summarize it more quickly by reading the rest of the editorial, dealing only in regard to the situation in Vancouver:
First the guns were torn from their positions, put on flat cars and started off for Vancouver to protect British Columbia and Ian Mackenzie's constituents against the yellow peril. Then somebody changed their mind, according to the reports, and the guns came trundling back again;
On top of all that, somebody began to rip out guns from emplacements at Vancouver and start them off for Halifax. Then that was stopped.
